        "title": "Masculine and feminine: le, la, un, une",
        "objective": "Name familiar classroom objects with un or une, and use le or la when pointing to a specific object.",
        "focus": "French nouns are grammatically masculine or feminine. Learn each object with its article: un stylo, une trousse. Use un/une when naming or introducing one object (C’est un cahier); use le/la for a particular object already identified (Voilà la gomme). The noun ending is only a partial gender clue, so learn the article with the noun. Hear the difference between nasal un and pronounced n in une, and between le and la.",
